000000\"><span class=\"s2049266DefaultParagraphFont\">The Supreme Court shall promulgate rules for the collection of outstanding court-ordered financial obligations through the administrative financial accountability system. The rules shall include graduated responses to noncompliance and a policy for the termination or adjustment of the financial obligations.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049266Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049266000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049266Normal\"><span class=\"s2049266SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049266SCL-000002\"><span>  <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2013/101/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2013, ch 101\">SL 2013, ch 101</a>, § 46, eff. Jan. 1, 2014; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2015/142/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2015, ch 142\">SL 2015, ch 142</a>, § 3.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2049267Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049267SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049267CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2049267Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049267DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049267000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049267SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049267SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049267Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-47-5\"><span class=\"s2049267SENU\">23A-47-5</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049267SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2049267CL\">Termination of financial obligation.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049267Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2049267DefaultParagraphFont\">Pursuant to rules established by the Supreme Court, any financial obligation from an order more than twenty-five years old, deemed uncollectible, or following the death of an offender may be terminated.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049267Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049267000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049267Normal\"><span class=\"s2049267SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049267SCL-000002\"><span>  <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2013/101/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2013, ch 101\">SL 2013, ch 101</a>, § 47, eff. Jan. 1, 2014.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" lang=\"en-US\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901Normal {\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: .001pt;\r\n}\r\nspan.sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901000000 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901DefaultParagraphFont-000001 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\"><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"SD 23A-47-5.1 - Termination of financial obligation--Death of party owing.\"><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"SDLRC Codified Law 23A-47-5.1 - Termination of financial obligation--Death of party owing.\"><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\"><meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/23A-47-5.1\"><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lawmakerdocuments.blob.core.usgovcloudapi.net/photos/logoshape.webp\"><meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"South Dakota Legislature\"></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes?Statute=23A-47-5.1\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901SENU\">23A-47-5.1</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901SENU\">. </span><span class=\"sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901CL\">Termination of financial obligation--Death of party owing.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901Normal\"><span class=\"sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901DefaultParagraphFont\">Any court-ordered financial obligation due and owing in a criminal proceeding, habeas corpus or abuse and neglect case, must be terminated three years following notice of death of the party owing the court-ordered financial obligation unless the court orders otherwise upon motion of the parties or victim. The Unified Judicial System shall provide the state’s attorney, county auditor and victim, if applicable, notice of the date of death when that information is received.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901000000\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901DefaultParagraphFont-000001\">Source:  </span><span class=\"sac8479f7bddd4dd4974fb2d30635d901SCL\"><span><a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2026/246/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2026, ch 246\">SL 2026, ch 246</a> (Supreme Court Rule 26-05), eff. July 1, 2026.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2049268Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049268SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049268CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2049268Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049268DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049268000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049268SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049268SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049268Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-47-6\"><span class=\"s2049268SENU\">23A-47-6</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049268SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2049268CL\">Failure to comply with plan of restitution or plan for financial obligations.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049268Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2049268DefaultParagraphFont\">Failure of any individual in this system to comply with the plan of restitution or plan for financial obligations as approved or modified by the court constitutes a violation of the conditions within this system. Without limitation, the court may modify the plan of restitution or financial obligation, extend the period of time for restitution or financial obligation, or continue the individual in the administrative financial accountability system. If the individual fails to make payment as ordered by the court, the individual may be held in contempt of the court's order.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049268Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049268000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049268Normal\"><span class=\"s2049268SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049268SCL-000002\"><span>  <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2013/101/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2013, ch 101\">SL 2013, ch 101</a>, § 48, eff. Jan. 1, 2014; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2015/142/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2015, ch 142\">SL 2015, ch 142</a>, § 4.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2049269Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049269SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049269CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2049269Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049269DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049269000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049269SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049269SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049269Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-47-7\"><span class=\"s2049269SENU\">23A-47-7</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049269SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2049269CL\">Contempt or review hearings.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049269Normal-000000\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049269DefaultParagraphFont\">The original sentencing court shall be the court of competent jurisdiction pursuant to § </span><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-47-6\"><span class=\"s2049269DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-47-6</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049269DefaultParagraphFont\"> for contempt or review hearings, if necessary, as part of the financial accountability collections system.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049269Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049269000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2049269Normal\"><span class=\"s2049269SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2049269SCL-000002\"><span>  <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2013/101/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2013, ch 101\">SL 2013, ch 101</a>, § 49, eff. Jan. 1, 2014; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2015/142/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2015, ch 142\">SL 2015, ch 142</a>, § 5.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2049270Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2049270SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    fon